## 7. What this guard does NOT cover (as hardened)

1. **Meaning of an exemption reason.** Only shape: ≥24 chars, ≥4 words, non-blank, no tab/newline, not one of ~30 placeholder tokens, contains 3 ASCII letters. Four nonsense words totalling 24 characters exempt any real regression (F1), and one such line covers three targets via `*` (F7).
2. **Root spellings Haxe accepts but the regex drops** — leading whitespace/tab, trailing whitespace, trailing CR (F2). No check compares the file's token set with Haxe's; `haxe` is not invoked.
3. **`--macro` side effects**, notably `Compiler.include`/`include('pkg')`, which add modules to one side only; also any other macro that changes what is compiled (F3). `--next`/`--each` multi-compilation files are likewise flattened into one root set.
4. **Classpath and library divergence.** `-cp`/`-lib` sets are unioned across all six files (F4: removing `-cp samples` from `swift-f32.hxml` passes). Per-file compilation reachability is not modelled.
5. **Roots removed from both files** unless the module declares `@:test` (F5). There is no pinned baseline root set to compare against.
6. **`@:test` modules outside `<guarded-cp>/tests`** — including two that already exist in-tree under the repo-root `tests/` (F10).
7. **Test ids, `@:test` case sets, module bodies, and runtime behaviour** under binary32 vs binary64 — the producer's own §7.1, unchanged. `samples/tests/f32/PrintedFloatTests.hx`'s 6 f32-only ids remain invisible here (declared in `tools/test-consistency/extra-id-allowlist.json`).
8. **Existence ≠ compilability.** The union + repo-wide fallback accepts a module no classpath provides (F9), and a root on the wrong target's classpath passes.
9. **The bypass surfaces are environmental.** `ROOTS_GUARD_ALLOWLIST` (undocumented) and `--repo-root`/`ROOTS_GUARD_REPO_ROOT` change what is checked; a caller who can set them can silence checks (F8, and the producer's §7.6).
10. **Not wired into CI.** `package.json` still only runs `bun tools/precision-guard/check.ts` in its verify chain (producer §7.11, re-checked), so none of this is enforced automatically; the guard is only as strong as the person who runs it with `--strict-duplicates`.
11. **`--help` is truncated** (F11), so the documented usage is not what a user sees from the flag.

